The KeyboardShortcut uses `react-native-key-command` `KeyCommand.addListener`, which on web uses its own DOM keydown listener. The important part is `bindHandlerToKeydownEvent` in index.ts (web): it ignores excluded nodes and `captureOnInputs`. It calls `event.preventDefault()` when callback.shouldPreventDefault.

Now, `useArrowKeyFocusManager` passes `excludedNodes: ['TEXTAREA']`. And PopoverMenu's Enter uses default captureOnInputs true.

