Actually I realize the key: the issue is about the quick action. The FAB shows a "quick action" option at the bottom with label "header". The `quickAction` onSelected calls `navigateToQuickAction`. Hmm.

Let me search for the exact issue text online from memory... "FAB menu - Pressing Enter doesn't open the selected option page". The fix might be PR #27004. 

Let me instead reason from the code. The likely bug is in `selectItem` in PopoverMenu. Let's compare with a known later version of PopoverMenu. I recall the later version's `selectItem`:

```js
const selectItem = (index: number) => {
    const selectedItem = currentMenuItems[index];

    if (selectedItem?.subMenuItems) {
        setCurrentMenuItems([...selectedItem.subMenuItems]);
        setEnteredSubMenuIndexes([...enteredSubMenuIndexes, index]);
        const selectedSubMenuItemIndex = selectedItem?.subMenuItems.findIndex((option) => option.isSelected);
        setFocusedIndex(selectedSubMenuItemIndex);
    } else if (selectedItem.shouldCallAfterModalHide && !Browser.isSafari()) {
        onItemSelected(selectedItem, index);
        Modal.close(
            () => {
                if (selectedItem.shouldCallAfterModalHide) {
                    selectedItem.onSelected?.();
                }
            },
            undefined,
            selectedItem.shouldCloseAllModals,
        );
    } else {
        onItemSelected(selectedItem, index);
        if (selectedItem.shouldCallAfterModalHide) {
            selectedItem.onSelected?.();
        }
    }
};
```

Hmm this matches. So the semantics: `onItemSelected` is expected to handle the selection. So for FAB, `onItemSelected={hideCreateMenu}` would be wrong (onSelected never called). But maybe FAB was recently refactored to use `onItemSelected` for both hiding and selection, and the fix is to make the FAB menu items call their onSelected.

Actually wait! Let me re-read the FAB `menuItems`. The items have `onSelected` and no `shouldCallAfterModalHide`. But maybe the intent is that `onItemSelected={hideCreateMenu}` hides the menu, and the item's `onSelected` is called separately... but it isn't. Hmm.

Actually, let me reconsider. Perhaps in the buggy version, the code DID call `selectedItem.onSelected?.()` unconditionally in the else branch, and the injected/real bug is that it got removed? But there's only one commit, so I can't compare.

